Enable VS Code Web Agents with a server-managed Agent Host and environment BYOK

1. Bundle and serve the Sessions web application as code-server's primary UI,
   while keeping the regular workbench available under `/editor/`.
2. Start and supervise one Agent Host from the VS Code server process, and
   expose its protocol and filesystem channels through the remote connection.
3. Add environment-backed OpenAI and Anthropic model adapters, including
   streaming tool calls and Anthropic/DeepSeek thinking blocks, without
   requiring GitHub authentication or falling back to subscription models.
4. Keep Agent Host sessions alive across browser disconnects and restore file,
   workspace, and progress links through the active remote authority.
5. Limit the Agents UI to the server-provided BYOK agent and configured models;
   retain the existing behavior for other VS Code web products.

